  "text": "-\nR-90-8\nA RESOLUTION ESTABLISHING RULES AND REGULATIONS FOR THE\nOPERATION OF SNOWMOBILES ON CLEAR CREEK COUNTY\nROADS #275, SILVER CREEK ROAD AND HARRIS DRIVE\nWHEREAS, the Clear Creek Board of County Commissioners\nis authorized by 33-14-110(3)(f) to enact a resolution\nestablishing snowmobile routes and to permit the operation of\nsnowmobiles on county roads; and\nWHEREAS,\nthe Board deems this Resolution to be in the\nbest interest of the citizens of Clear Creek County;\nNOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED, by the Clear Creek Board\nof County Commissioners that snowmobiles shall be permitted\nto operate on the following county roads:\n1.\nBeginning at a point where County Road #275 intersects\nPine Way and the southern boundary line of Unit 1, St.\nMary's subdivision; thence north along County Road #275\nto the point of intersection with Lake Road, which is\nthe approximate point\nof entry for the St. Mary's\nGlacier Ski Area on the west side of County Road #275;\n2.\nThat part of Silver Creek Road from the point of\nintersection of Silver Creek Road\nand County Road #275\nto the point of intersection of Silver Creek Road and\nTexas Drive; and\n3.\nThat part of Harris Drive from the point of intersection\nof Harris Drive\nTexas Drive to the point of\nintersection of Harris Drive and Alice Road.\nBE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that such use shall be subject\nto the following rules and regulations:\n1.\nSnowmobile Operation:\nAll snowmobiles shall be operated\nstate and\nincal ordar e wiche and somobiee fider; instare ular,\nbut not exclusively, Section 33-14-101 et seg., C.R.S.,\nand Titles 16, 25 and 42 of the Colorado Revised\nStatutes.\n2.\nApplication:\nThese Regulations shall apply exclusively\nto snowmobiles and\nshall not apply to any other\nmotorized vehicles or other all-terrain vehicles.\n3.\n4.\nRoads:\nThe roads described above shall be open for use\nby snowmobiles, but such use shall not be exclusive.\nAll snowmobiles shall be used only upon the roads\ndescribed above, marked for such use.\nSafety Warning Flag: All snowmobiles shall carry a\ndesignated orange warning flag attached to a flexible\npole affixed to the back of each snowmobile.\n5.\nSigns: All snowmobiles shall be operated in accordance\nwith\nall snowmobile signs; in addition to any other\ntraffic signs appearing on the designated snowmobile\nroute.\n6.\nAll snowmobiles shall be driven as far to the\nright shoulder of the road as possible; and shall be\ndriven in single file.\n7.\nSpeed Limit:\nThe speed limit for snowmobiles shall be\nthat speed\nlimit governing other motor vehicles, unless\notherwise posted.",
  "text_sha256": "657aee59a9955df85e7f79d20d749c35f15fd786ca44ae333427955970e50cc4",
